{title: Sweet Hour of Prayer}
{artist: William W. Walford / William B. Bradbury}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{key_original: D}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Sweet hour of prayer! [D]sweet hour of [G]prayer!
That [C]calls me from a [G]world of [D]care
And [G]bids me at my [C]Father's [G]throne
Make [Am]all my wants and [D]wishes [G]known
In [G]seasons of dis[D]tress and [G]grief
My [C]soul has often [G]found re[D]lief
And [G]oft escaped the [C]tempter's [G]snare
By [Am]thy re[D]turn, sweet [G]hour of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Sweet hour of prayer! [D]sweet hour of [G]prayer!
The [C]joys I feel, the [G]bliss I [D]share
Of [G]those whose anxious [C]spirits [G]burn
With [Am]strong desires for [D]thy re[G]turn
With [G]such I hasten [D]to the [G]place
Where [C]God my Savior [G]shows His [D]face
And [G]gladly take my [C]station [G]there
And [Am]wait for [D]thee, sweet [G]hour of prayer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Sweet hour of prayer! [D]sweet hour of [G]prayer!
Thy [C]wings shall my pe[G]tition [D]bear
To [G]Him whose truth and [C]faithful[G]ness
En[Am]gage the waiting [D]soul to [G]bless
And [G]since He bids me [D]seek His [G]face
Be[C]lieve His Word and [G]trust His [D]grace
I'll [G]cast on Him my [C]every [G]care
And [Am]wait for [D]thee, sweet [G]hour of prayer
{end_of_verse}
